# LF everywhere. A CRLF checkout on Windows breaks shell scripts the moment
# they are mounted into a Linux container, and the failure reads as "the
# container is broken" rather than "your checkout has \r line endings".
#
# MEASURED, not inherited: `bash -n scripts/start.sh` -- the CI step that
# exists precisely so a broken start.sh fails here rather than inside
# `docker compose logs` -- reports
#     syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
# against a CRLF copy of that file. Without this, adding windows-latest to
# the matrix turns that step red on every run.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.whl binary
